  << /ActualText (Develop a clear and consistent meaning of the values discovered\054 not necessarily a universal analysis\056\240\n\240\nEthical and political values \050such as justice\054 fairness\054 privacy\054 tolerance\054 autonomy\054 and liberty\051 are conceptually abstract\054 controversial\054 and notoriously difficult to define\056 Yet when we reach for them to describe a political system\054 a relationship\054 an organization\054 or a competition\054 we have in mind definitions or interpretations that are concrete\054 specific\054 and operational\056 Transforming a value from an abstraction to a fully articulated concept makes it accessible to design and capable of influencing architecture and features\056 It is the work of definition and analysis that forms a necessary bridge between abstract value concepts and concretely articulated conceptualizations able to guide a designer\031s hand\056\n\nThe designer also must be guided by a sound and reflective grasp of the value concept\056\n\240\nWell\055defined concepts \050privacy\054 openness\054 or any other value at play\051 are of more than philosophical interest\072 they have genuine consequences for the technologies in our lives\056)
     /K [ 1395 ]
     /P 6104 0 R
     /Pg 3315 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

